WEBVTT

1
00:00:18,404 --> 00:00:21,074
(ominous music)

2
00:00:32,230 --> 00:00:33,931
(clock ticking)

3
00:00:33,933 --> 00:00:36,906
(curtain flapping)

4
00:00:38,242 --> 00:00:41,850
- Once there was
a boy named James,

5
00:00:43,118 --> 00:00:44,456
my grandson,

6
00:00:45,858 --> 00:00:48,831
a child who learned the weight
of goodbye far too young.

7
00:00:51,234 --> 00:00:54,940
After his parents died,
he came to live with me

8
00:00:54,942 --> 00:00:58,415
in a house of old wood
and ticking clocks.

9
00:00:58,417 --> 00:01:00,017
(thunder rumbling)

10
00:01:00,019 --> 00:01:02,321
A house full of memory.

11
00:01:02,323 --> 00:01:05,696
(clock ticking)

12
00:01:05,698 --> 00:01:07,669
Then death is a greedy visitor.

13
00:01:08,571 --> 00:01:11,407
It never comes just once.

14
00:01:11,409 --> 00:01:13,009
It returned

15
00:01:13,011 --> 00:01:15,115
and it took his
very best friend.

16
00:01:16,954 --> 00:01:18,691
I watched the boy's heart break.

17
00:01:19,893 --> 00:01:23,397
So then I made a vow.

18
00:01:23,399 --> 00:01:27,006
You will never
lose anyone again.

19
00:01:28,308 --> 00:01:29,210
I worked.

20
00:01:30,413 --> 00:01:33,216
I spent more and more
time in the basement,

21
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:34,956
a place forbidden to James.

22
00:01:36,224 --> 00:01:38,862
Days turned to weeks

23
00:01:38,864 --> 00:01:41,000
creating something,

24
00:01:41,002 --> 00:01:43,404
something just for him.

25
00:01:43,406 --> 00:01:46,478
Something which will
never say goodbye.

26
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:49,250
Something which will
never belong to death.

27
00:01:52,089 --> 00:01:52,992
Pinocchio.

28
00:01:55,062 --> 00:01:56,329
(letters rattling)

29
00:01:56,331 --> 00:01:59,304
(mysterious music)

30
00:02:07,989 --> 00:02:11,360
(James knocking on door)

31
00:02:11,362 --> 00:02:12,563
Not today. Thanks.

32
00:02:12,565 --> 00:02:14,265
- Oh gosh, no, not again.

33
00:02:14,267 --> 00:02:15,736
No. Come on.

34
00:02:15,738 --> 00:02:17,707
This joke is so old it
should be in a nursing home.

35
00:02:17,709 --> 00:02:18,474
(Mia laughs)

36
00:02:18,476 --> 00:02:19,746
- [Mia] Um, Bye James.

37
00:02:25,189 --> 00:02:26,591
- How's he holding up?

38
00:02:26,593 --> 00:02:27,860
- [Mia] Oh, he had
a moment earlier,

39
00:02:27,862 --> 00:02:29,731
but I think he'll be okay.

40
00:02:29,733 --> 00:02:30,766
- And you?

41
00:02:30,768 --> 00:02:32,134
- I'm good as can be.

42
00:02:32,136 --> 00:02:33,171
Yeah, thanks.

43
00:02:33,941 --> 00:02:35,240
Bye.

44
00:02:35,242 --> 00:02:36,379
- Thanks for keeping
an eye on him lately.

45
00:02:37,615 --> 00:02:40,788
(light solemn music)

46
00:02:45,631 --> 00:02:46,463
(birds chirping)

47
00:02:46,465 --> 00:02:47,869
- Zach, wait up.

48
00:02:50,106 --> 00:02:52,912
(dramatic music)

49
00:02:57,655 --> 00:03:00,225
(door creaks)

50
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:05,703
- Grab your coat, kiddo.

51
00:03:05,705 --> 00:03:08,107
Bit of fresh air
will do us good.

52
00:03:08,109 --> 00:03:08,911
Now come on.

53
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:16,459
It's always hard losing
someone you love.

54
00:03:17,527 --> 00:03:18,997
Your mother, now
your best friend.

55
00:03:21,502 --> 00:03:25,210
- Do you ever worry, Granddad,
about what happens after?

56
00:03:26,980 --> 00:03:29,151
Like, when we die.

57
00:03:30,319 --> 00:03:32,157
- All I worry about is you.

58
00:03:35,230 --> 00:03:37,702
- I just, I wish
Zach was still here.

59
00:03:38,670 --> 00:03:40,173
It doesn't feel
the same anymore.

60
00:03:41,509 --> 00:03:43,276
- Well, maybe he is.

61
00:03:43,278 --> 00:03:46,150
(gentle piano music)

62
00:03:46,152 --> 00:03:48,288
I believe what makes you, you,

63
00:03:49,626 --> 00:03:52,364
sticks around after and
moves into what surrounds us.

64
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:56,438
- Yeah, Dudley told me
that stuff's rubbish.

65
00:03:57,574 --> 00:03:59,911
- I've seen Dudley pick
his nose and eat it too.

66
00:03:59,913 --> 00:04:02,883
(both laughing)

67
00:04:02,885 --> 00:04:03,787
Look up.

68
00:04:05,390 --> 00:04:08,127
What do you see?

69
00:04:08,129 --> 00:04:09,933
- Um, loads of stars.

70
00:04:11,302 --> 00:04:14,306
- "There are more things in
heaven and earth, Horatio,

71
00:04:14,308 --> 00:04:16,478
"than are dreamt of
in your philosophy."

72
00:04:19,619 --> 00:04:22,925
It means life is full of
endless possibilities.

73
00:04:23,861 --> 00:04:26,432
(light music)

74
00:04:27,969 --> 00:04:30,037
(Geppetto coughing)

75
00:04:30,039 --> 00:04:31,440
- Granddad, are you okay?

76
00:04:31,442 --> 00:04:32,810
Are you okay? Do you want me to-

77
00:04:32,812 --> 00:04:34,246
- I'm fine. Don't worry.

78
00:04:34,248 --> 00:04:35,081
- You sure?

79
00:04:35,083 --> 00:04:36,651
- Mm.

80
00:04:36,653 --> 00:04:37,554
Fine.

81
00:04:40,393 --> 00:04:42,295
We should get home soon.

82
00:04:42,297 --> 00:04:46,706
I have something very
exciting to show you tomorrow.

83
00:04:48,609 --> 00:04:51,582
(mysterious music)

84
00:05:16,065 --> 00:05:18,704
(floor creaks)

85
00:05:28,022 --> 00:05:31,095
(suspenseful music)

86
00:05:48,162 --> 00:05:51,403
(footsteps pattering)

87
00:05:52,570 --> 00:05:55,143
(door creaks)

88
00:06:06,665 --> 00:06:09,405
(ominous music)

89
00:06:12,177 --> 00:06:15,583
(light switch clicking)

90
00:06:18,055 --> 00:06:21,061
(suspenseful music)

91
00:06:22,765 --> 00:06:25,571
(dramatic music)

92
00:06:28,810 --> 00:06:30,445
(ominous music)

93
00:06:30,447 --> 00:06:33,619
(footsteps thudding)

94
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:38,193
(door creaking)

95
00:06:38,195 --> 00:06:41,168
(door clicks shut)

96
00:06:42,438 --> 00:06:45,511
(suspenseful music)

97
00:07:04,214 --> 00:07:06,486
You sure there's nothing
else you remember?

98
00:07:08,957 --> 00:07:10,124
(stairs creak)

99
00:07:10,126 --> 00:07:11,028
James?

100
00:07:12,431 --> 00:07:13,732
- Who are you talking to?

101
00:07:14,635 --> 00:07:15,902
- Come down.

102
00:07:15,904 --> 00:07:17,338
There's someone here
I want you to meet.

103
00:07:17,340 --> 00:07:18,641
- Someone?

104
00:07:18,643 --> 00:07:19,612
- Come, come.

105
00:07:21,516 --> 00:07:25,154
(mysterious music)

106
00:07:25,156 --> 00:07:26,924
- Is that what I saw upstairs?

107
00:07:26,926 --> 00:07:27,962
- That'll be him.

108
00:07:31,469 --> 00:07:32,603
- Where is he?

109
00:07:32,605 --> 00:07:34,573
(ominous music)

110
00:07:34,575 --> 00:07:35,577
- In there.

111
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:38,349
He's shy, I think.

112
00:07:39,452 --> 00:07:41,821
(ominous music)

113
00:07:41,823 --> 00:07:42,757
Come on out.

114
00:07:43,792 --> 00:07:45,196
I want you to meet someone.

115
00:07:46,331 --> 00:07:48,601
He's the boy I've been
telling you about.

116
00:07:48,603 --> 00:07:50,505
(ominous music)

117
00:07:50,507 --> 00:07:53,645
(Pinocchio's hand creaking)

118
00:07:53,647 --> 00:07:54,548
Yes, him.

119
00:07:55,783 --> 00:07:58,523
(ominous music)

120
00:08:05,404 --> 00:08:06,437
(water splashes)

121
00:08:06,439 --> 00:08:09,412
(mysterious music)

122
00:08:12,016 --> 00:08:14,855
(dramatic music)

123
00:08:22,871 --> 00:08:25,274
You're the first
person he's seen

124
00:08:25,276 --> 00:08:26,178
other than me.

125
00:08:33,626 --> 00:08:36,632
I think he wants
to be your friend.

126
00:08:41,208 --> 00:08:43,076
(dramatic music)

127
00:08:43,078 --> 00:08:44,045
- Stop! Go away!

128
00:08:44,047 --> 00:08:45,116
Please stop!

129
00:08:47,086 --> 00:08:48,322
- James, stop!

130
00:08:51,429 --> 00:08:54,633
(James panting)

131
00:08:54,635 --> 00:08:55,971
Listen to me, James.

132
00:08:56,873 --> 00:08:58,975
- What the fuck was that?

133
00:08:58,977 --> 00:09:00,244
- Calm down and
watch your language-

134
00:09:00,246 --> 00:09:01,480
- No, no, no, no!

135
00:09:01,482 --> 00:09:02,582
What was that? That
thing down there?

136
00:09:02,584 --> 00:09:03,718
What? What is it?

137
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:04,553
- It's not a thing.

138
00:09:04,555 --> 00:09:06,022
It's a who, James.

139
00:09:06,024 --> 00:09:07,093
It's alive.

140
00:09:10,099 --> 00:09:12,469
Things aren't always
what they seem,

141
00:09:12,471 --> 00:09:14,908
life is not-
- What were you talking about?

142
00:09:14,910 --> 00:09:16,276
- I know it's hard to believe,

143
00:09:16,278 --> 00:09:19,248
but trust me in time, this
is all gonna make sense.

144
00:09:19,250 --> 00:09:20,687
I didn't mean to scare you.

145
00:09:21,789 --> 00:09:23,693
I just thought you
could use a friend.

146
00:09:24,728 --> 00:09:25,630
I know he could.

147
00:09:27,668 --> 00:09:28,570
- A friend?

148
00:09:29,505 --> 00:09:30,674
With, with that thing?

149
00:09:34,247 --> 00:09:36,919
- [Geppetto] This could be
good for the both of you.

150
00:09:46,004 --> 00:09:48,810
(dramatic music)

151
00:09:54,153 --> 00:09:55,990
- How long has he
been down there?

152
00:09:55,992 --> 00:09:58,028
- [Geppetto] That's all
he's ever really known.

153
00:09:59,230 --> 00:10:01,767
(door creaks)

154
00:10:01,769 --> 00:10:03,671
Why don't you say hello?

155
00:10:03,673 --> 00:10:06,646
(mysterious music)

156
00:10:08,984 --> 00:10:09,885
- James.

157
00:10:10,921 --> 00:10:11,822
- I'm Pinocchio.

158
00:10:13,626 --> 00:10:14,826
Are we friends?

159
00:10:14,828 --> 00:10:16,164
- Maybe. We'll see.

160
00:10:19,038 --> 00:10:19,939
- James,

161
00:10:21,409 --> 00:10:23,209
you can tell nobody about this.

162
00:10:23,211 --> 00:10:24,080
Understood?

163
00:10:28,690 --> 00:10:29,592
Good boy.

164
00:10:31,028 --> 00:10:33,965
(mysterious music)

165
00:10:33,967 --> 00:10:35,468
(playful music)

166
00:10:35,470 --> 00:10:37,706
- You're not gonna get
my ship, Captain James.

167
00:10:37,708 --> 00:10:39,445
- Oh, I'm gonna make
you walk the plank.

168
00:10:40,647 --> 00:10:42,281
Okay. You got it?

169
00:10:42,283 --> 00:10:43,386
- [Pinocchio] Mm-hmm.

170
00:10:45,924 --> 00:10:46,993
- Your move.

171
00:10:49,932 --> 00:10:53,271
(chess pieces clatter)

172
00:10:54,307 --> 00:10:56,777
(bright music)

173
00:10:56,779 --> 00:10:59,716
- Is that me?

174
00:10:59,718 --> 00:11:00,918
- Yeah.

175
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:02,055
(cellphone buzzing)

176
00:11:02,057 --> 00:11:02,858
Now.

177
00:11:04,193 --> 00:11:05,662
- Dude.

178
00:11:05,664 --> 00:11:08,367
What the fuck is that?

179
00:11:08,369 --> 00:11:09,836
- [James] Nothing. Nothing.

180
00:11:09,838 --> 00:11:11,507
It's just a doll Granddad made.

181
00:11:11,509 --> 00:11:12,644
This one's biology.

182
00:11:13,846 --> 00:11:15,383
- [Pinocchio] What is bilology?

183
00:11:17,487 --> 00:11:20,290
- It's like why boys are
made different from you.

184
00:11:20,292 --> 00:11:22,095
Organs and stuff.

185
00:11:22,097 --> 00:11:24,366
- (gasps) Wow.

186
00:11:24,368 --> 00:11:25,870
What else makes us different?

187
00:11:27,206 --> 00:11:30,111
- Teeth, eyes, hair, skin.

188
00:11:30,113 --> 00:11:31,916
I mean, there's lots of things.

189
00:11:32,718 --> 00:11:34,886
- I wanna be just like you.

190
00:11:34,888 --> 00:11:36,222
- (laughs) No, trust me.

191
00:11:36,224 --> 00:11:37,257
You don't.

192
00:11:37,259 --> 00:11:38,629
You're way cooler than me.

193
00:11:40,834 --> 00:11:42,269
- What's this?

194
00:11:43,139 --> 00:11:44,040
- Oh.

195
00:11:46,212 --> 00:11:50,885
Uh...

196
00:11:50,887 --> 00:11:54,126
- [TV Narrator] As the herd
follows the sea's plains,

197
00:11:54,128 --> 00:11:55,864
danger lies in wait.

198
00:11:57,333 --> 00:11:59,669
But in the presence
of a predator,

199
00:11:59,671 --> 00:12:02,009
the herd will
protect one another.

200
00:12:03,679 --> 00:12:05,416
- The herd will protect.

201
00:12:06,652 --> 00:12:10,292
(buffalo grunting onscreen)

202
00:12:11,962 --> 00:12:12,764
You are my herd.

203
00:12:14,234 --> 00:12:15,968
(mysterious music)

204
00:12:15,970 --> 00:12:20,413
- [TV Narrator] However,
sometimes the greatest danger

205
00:12:21,448 --> 00:12:23,853
comes from within the group.

206
00:12:25,390 --> 00:12:28,661
(door creaks)

207
00:12:28,663 --> 00:12:31,969
(lion growls onscreen)

208
00:12:37,314 --> 00:12:40,685
(mysterious music)

209
00:12:40,687 --> 00:12:42,424
- [Pinocchio] James.

210
00:12:45,997 --> 00:12:46,897
Why?

211
00:12:46,899 --> 00:12:48,567
- You can't.

212
00:12:48,569 --> 00:12:50,204
- I want to be with James.

213
00:12:50,206 --> 00:12:51,907
- He's going to school tomorrow.

214
00:12:51,909 --> 00:12:53,811
People won't react well.

215
00:12:53,813 --> 00:12:55,450
- Because I don't have a penis?

216
00:12:56,552 --> 00:12:59,524
- No, I don't know
what to say to that.

217
00:13:00,426 --> 00:13:02,228
The world isn't ready for you.

218
00:13:02,230 --> 00:13:03,631
Not yet.

219
00:13:03,633 --> 00:13:06,373
(ominous music)

220
00:13:10,012 --> 00:13:12,682
- Like 100 kg.
- Rubbish, mate.

221
00:13:12,684 --> 00:13:14,452
- Pure muscle, it's just hidden.

222
00:13:14,454 --> 00:13:17,292
Just need to do, like, a diet.

223
00:13:17,294 --> 00:13:18,527
- Need some help with that?

224
00:13:18,529 --> 00:13:19,829
- You can do that?

225
00:13:19,831 --> 00:13:21,867
- [James] I could help you
lose five pounds, easy.

226
00:13:21,869 --> 00:13:22,835
- How?

227
00:13:22,837 --> 00:13:24,506
- I just cut off a right arm.

228
00:13:24,508 --> 00:13:25,375
- Ah!

229
00:13:25,377 --> 00:13:27,578
(James laughing)

230
00:13:27,580 --> 00:13:30,553
(inhaler whooshes)

231
00:13:32,089 --> 00:13:34,895
(insect buzzing)

232
00:13:36,231 --> 00:13:37,200
- Ah! Fuck!

233
00:13:38,669 --> 00:13:42,076
(groans) Ouch, my head.

234
00:13:48,723 --> 00:13:51,795
(suspenseful music)

235
00:13:54,066 --> 00:13:57,139
(Pinocchio exhales)

236
00:13:58,242 --> 00:14:01,248
(mysterious music)

237
00:14:12,937 --> 00:14:15,743
(Pinocchio gasps)

238
00:14:16,812 --> 00:14:20,487
(mysterious music continues)

239
00:14:25,329 --> 00:14:28,636
(electricity crackles)

240
00:14:36,285 --> 00:14:37,618
(dramatic music)

241
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:40,925
(Pinocchio gasps)

242
00:14:40,927 --> 00:14:42,730
- Child, come closer.

243
00:14:44,133 --> 00:14:45,703
My splinters hurt.

244
00:14:46,506 --> 00:14:48,907
- You talk?

245
00:14:48,909 --> 00:14:52,784
- Who else would tell
the truth he hides?

246
00:14:54,321 --> 00:14:56,491
- What are you?

247
00:14:56,493 --> 00:14:59,530
- I am your Wood Mother.

248
00:14:59,532 --> 00:15:03,270
Geppetto may have
carved our bodies,

249
00:15:03,272 --> 00:15:05,341
but I will shape your mind.

250
00:15:05,343 --> 00:15:06,745
- Are you stuck there?

251
00:15:07,714 --> 00:15:08,682
- As are you.

252
00:15:10,653 --> 00:15:11,653
- I'm not stuck.

253
00:15:11,655 --> 00:15:13,957
- The strings may be invisible,

254
00:15:13,959 --> 00:15:16,228
but you are still his puppet.

255
00:15:16,230 --> 00:15:17,965
- I'm no puppet.

256
00:15:17,967 --> 00:15:20,203
I'm just like James.

257
00:15:20,205 --> 00:15:21,308
I'm a real boy.

258
00:15:23,946 --> 00:15:28,188
- (laughs) Your
nose betrays you.

259
00:15:29,659 --> 00:15:31,893
The creator says you are real.

260
00:15:31,895 --> 00:15:35,537
He doesn't look
at you like James.

261
00:15:36,673 --> 00:15:41,212
You want his arms to
hold you, not hide you,

262
00:15:41,214 --> 00:15:42,082
then come closer

263
00:15:43,553 --> 00:15:46,992
and I'll whisper how to be real.

264
00:15:48,027 --> 00:15:51,234
You need skin,
blood, teeth, hair.

265
00:15:52,102 --> 00:15:54,373
Take them, wear them.

266
00:15:54,375 --> 00:15:55,874
- Ew, that's disgusting.

267
00:15:55,876 --> 00:15:56,876
I'm not doing that.

268
00:15:56,878 --> 00:15:59,949
(Wood Mother laughing)

269
00:15:59,951 --> 00:16:04,057
- Then stay caged,
little puppet,

270
00:16:04,059 --> 00:16:07,635
whilst James walks in sunlight.

271
00:16:08,769 --> 00:16:10,038
Unless I'm wrong.

272
00:16:11,676 --> 00:16:12,578
Prove it.

273
00:16:13,546 --> 00:16:15,046
(dramatic music)

274
00:16:15,048 --> 00:16:16,717
(glass shatters)

275
00:16:16,719 --> 00:16:19,358
(bright music)

276
00:16:31,382 --> 00:16:32,282
- Wow.

277
00:16:34,455 --> 00:16:37,292
