(jaunty big band music)

1098
01:00:57,378 --> 01:01:00,314
♪ Oh, you beautiful doll ♪

1099
01:01:00,316 --> 01:01:04,023
♪ You great big beautiful doll ♪

1100
01:01:04,025 --> 01:01:08,330
♪ Let me put my
arms around you ♪

1101
01:01:08,332 --> 01:01:12,739
♪ I could never
live without you ♪

1102
01:01:12,741 --> 01:01:15,512
♪ Oh, you beautiful doll ♪

1103
01:01:15,514 --> 01:01:19,086
♪ You great big beautiful doll ♪

1104
01:01:19,088 --> 01:01:23,193
♪ If you ever leave me
how my heart will ache ♪

1105
01:01:23,195 --> 01:01:27,969
♪ I wanna hug you,
but I need a break ♪

1106
01:01:27,971 --> 01:01:30,909
♪ Oh, oh, oh, oh ♪

1107
01:01:30,911 --> 01:01:32,244
- Hmm, what do you think?

1108
01:01:32,246 --> 01:01:34,683
This hat suit me, Pinocch?

1109
01:01:34,685 --> 01:01:38,093
(jaunty big band music)

1110
01:01:52,855 --> 01:01:55,927
(suspenseful music)

1111
01:02:00,035 --> 01:02:03,141
(door creaks)

1112
01:02:03,143 --> 01:02:06,047
(insects buzzing)

1113
01:02:07,551 --> 01:02:10,524
(suspenseful music)

1114
01:02:20,243 --> 01:02:22,011
(ominous music)

1115
01:02:22,013 --> 01:02:24,985
(blood squelching)

1116
01:02:33,503 --> 01:02:36,041
- [Pinocchio] Look, Father,
I made a puppet too.

1117
01:02:40,717 --> 01:02:43,456
(ominous music)

1118
01:02:47,865 --> 01:02:49,435
- Is that your granddad's car?

1119
01:02:50,770 --> 01:02:52,104
- [Dudley] Oh yeah.
There he goes.

1120
01:02:52,106 --> 01:02:54,509
- James.
- Off to wreck more lives.

1121
01:02:54,511 --> 01:02:55,745
- Pinocchio.

1122
01:02:55,747 --> 01:02:57,749
Quick, Mia. Go after him.

1123
01:02:57,751 --> 01:02:58,887
- [Dudley] They're both killers.

1124
01:03:00,957 --> 01:03:02,893
(tires screeching)

1125
01:03:02,895 --> 01:03:04,095
Oh!

1126
01:03:04,097 --> 01:03:07,170
(suspenseful music)

1127
01:03:08,740 --> 01:03:13,816
(Pinocchio's body thudding)
(Pinocchio shouting)

1128
01:03:15,085 --> 01:03:17,089
- They were going to hurt James.

1129
01:03:20,398 --> 01:03:23,133
(footsteps thudding)

1130
01:03:23,135 --> 01:03:24,770
But why?
(door slams shut)

1131
01:03:24,772 --> 01:03:26,139
(Wood Mother laughing)

1132
01:03:26,141 --> 01:03:29,382
Why, that nasty, lying bitch.

1133
01:03:30,250 --> 01:03:31,151
You lied to me.

1134
01:03:32,086 --> 01:03:34,189
Why did you lie to me?

1135
01:03:34,191 --> 01:03:38,931
- Messed up, haven't
you, little splinter?

1136
01:03:38,933 --> 01:03:41,203
- This is all your fault.

1137
01:03:41,205 --> 01:03:45,678
- You carved this path yourself.

1138
01:03:45,680 --> 01:03:49,151
- You got me to do
those bad things.

1139
01:03:49,153 --> 01:03:51,957
I'm not gonna let
you trick me anymore.

1140
01:03:51,959 --> 01:03:52,861
- Greedy.

1141
01:03:54,030 --> 01:03:56,936
Dissatisfied with what you are.

1142
01:03:57,904 --> 01:04:00,842
I should be where you are!

1143
01:04:00,844 --> 01:04:03,814
Look at me when I'm speaking!

1144
01:04:03,816 --> 01:04:05,718
- You've made everyone hate me.

1145
01:04:05,720 --> 01:04:10,193
- Because you're bad, Pinocchio.

1146
01:04:10,195 --> 01:04:13,669
Bad as the ones you butchered.

1147
01:04:14,838 --> 01:04:18,176
- We raised you to be
a good boy, Pinocch.

1148
01:04:18,178 --> 01:04:22,552
- Oh, get off me,
Cricket! (groans)

1149
01:04:22,554 --> 01:04:23,788
There you are!

1150
01:04:23,790 --> 01:04:24,923
(Pinocchio shouting)

1151
01:04:24,925 --> 01:04:26,960
- Don't you dare!
(mallet thuds)

1152
01:04:26,962 --> 01:04:29,031
- Leave him alone!

1153
01:04:29,033 --> 01:04:30,802
- No! You dumb bitch!

1154
01:04:30,804 --> 01:04:31,770
(dramatic music)

1155
01:04:31,772 --> 01:04:32,906
Nasty Wood Mother!

1156
01:04:32,908 --> 01:04:36,246
I'll teach you,
you stupid asshole!

1157
01:04:36,248 --> 01:04:37,450
Wrinkly shit!

1158
01:04:37,452 --> 01:04:39,686
(Wood Mother shouting)

1159
01:04:39,688 --> 01:04:43,462
(mallet thudding)
(Pinocchio yelling)

1160
01:04:43,464 --> 01:04:45,466
(Wood Mother gasping)

1161
01:04:45,468 --> 01:04:49,507
(Pinocchio breathing heavily)

1162
01:04:49,509 --> 01:04:52,314
(water dripping)

1163
01:05:06,308 --> 01:05:08,614
- There's something
I need to show you.

1164
01:05:13,923 --> 01:05:16,363
You want to be real
because of your past.

1165
01:05:20,002 --> 01:05:21,169
Come with me.

1166
01:05:21,171 --> 01:05:23,676
(door creaks)

1167
01:05:28,587 --> 01:05:30,489
- [Pinocchio] What
is this place?

1168
01:05:30,491 --> 01:05:32,628
- [Geppetto] It's
where you were created.

1169
01:05:35,434 --> 01:05:39,271
(switch clangs)
(electricity zaps)

1170
01:05:39,273 --> 01:05:41,444
- [Pinocchio] Oh my God.

1171
01:05:41,446 --> 01:05:44,452
(mysterious music)

1172
01:05:55,305 --> 01:05:58,044
(ominous music)

1173
01:06:02,754 --> 01:06:05,324
- It feeds through the roots,

1174
01:06:05,326 --> 01:06:08,398
growing as it siphons
their life force

1175
01:06:08,400 --> 01:06:10,704
infusing itself into the wood.

1176
01:06:12,239 --> 01:06:14,878
The same wood I then harvest.

1177
01:06:20,222 --> 01:06:21,591
That's right.

1178
01:06:21,593 --> 01:06:24,896
(dramatic music)

1179
01:06:24,898 --> 01:06:29,975
(mallet thudding)
(wood splintering)

1180
01:06:34,585 --> 01:06:36,721
You are the mere existence.

1181
01:06:36,723 --> 01:06:38,794
When their life
ended, yours began.

1182
01:06:40,431 --> 01:06:41,698
(ominous music)

1183
01:06:41,700 --> 01:06:43,101
- Where did they come from?

1184
01:06:45,641 --> 01:06:48,411
(ominous music)

1185
01:06:48,413 --> 01:06:50,983
(crow cawing)

1186
01:06:54,826 --> 01:06:57,997
(footsteps thudding)

1187
01:07:00,068 --> 01:07:01,804
(ominous music)

1188
01:07:01,806 --> 01:07:04,945
- Once I realized I
could harvest it, I
began to study them.

1189
01:07:06,583 --> 01:07:09,886
Trying to understand
how they worked,

1190
01:07:09,888 --> 01:07:12,092
trying to perfect the process.

1191
01:07:15,366 --> 01:07:18,136
There were many failures.

1192
01:07:18,138 --> 01:07:19,475
- [Pinocchio] It's moving.

1193
01:07:22,648 --> 01:07:25,183
- One of which was
particularly dangerous.

1194
01:07:25,185 --> 01:07:26,118
(puppet growling)

1195
01:07:26,120 --> 01:07:27,989
So I had to keep it locked away.

1196
01:07:27,991 --> 01:07:33,067
(puppet growling)
(ominous music)

1197
01:07:34,236 --> 01:07:36,707
But then you came along,

1198
01:07:36,709 --> 01:07:39,077
my perfect creation.

1199
01:07:39,079 --> 01:07:40,849
You had so much potential.

1200
01:07:40,851 --> 01:07:41,820
- Potential?

1201
01:07:43,890 --> 01:07:45,492
For what?

1202
01:07:45,494 --> 01:07:47,930
- To prove that I was right.

1203
01:07:47,932 --> 01:07:49,399
That we could be reborn.

1204
01:07:49,401 --> 01:07:51,204
That we can master death.

1205
01:07:54,545 --> 01:07:58,451
But ultimately you're as much
a failure as the rest of them.

1206
01:07:58,453 --> 01:07:59,354
- Oh.

1207
01:08:06,401 --> 01:08:08,437
- [Dudley] Your granddad
is a killer, James.

1208
01:08:08,439 --> 01:08:11,342
What could we do
against a killer?

1209
01:08:11,344 --> 01:08:13,781
- You're absolutely sure?
- Yes.

1210
01:08:13,783 --> 01:08:14,917
You saw what he did
to that other doll.

1211
01:08:14,919 --> 01:08:17,789
He doesn't deserve to die, okay?

1212
01:08:17,791 --> 01:08:20,629
- James, like, maybe
it's better if he does.

1213
01:08:20,631 --> 01:08:21,864
- I agree. Dudley's right.

1214
01:08:21,866 --> 01:08:24,369
- He was doing it to protect me!

1215
01:08:24,371 --> 01:08:25,607
- [Dudley] But your granddad
is a murderer, James.

1216
01:08:26,809 --> 01:08:29,079
- Whatever, stay here then.
- Stop.

1217
01:08:32,052 --> 01:08:33,857
Not listening at all, are you?

1218
01:08:35,325 --> 01:08:38,298
(mysterious music)

1219
01:08:43,274 --> 01:08:44,411
- It's strange.

1220
01:08:45,581 --> 01:08:48,486
Both of us wanting to
be like each other.

1221
01:08:49,956 --> 01:08:51,859
- Who did I come from?

1222
01:08:53,261 --> 01:08:54,496
- A young boy.

1223
01:08:54,498 --> 01:08:56,534
A dear friend of James'.

1224
01:08:56,536 --> 01:08:57,838
- (gasps) Zach?

1225
01:08:59,407 --> 01:09:00,744
- Pinocchio came from

1226
01:09:01,746 --> 01:09:03,346
Zach?

1227
01:09:03,348 --> 01:09:04,417
- What the hell?

1228
01:09:07,758 --> 01:09:10,226
- I'd hoped Zach and
James' friendship

1229
01:09:10,228 --> 01:09:12,868
would show that
death isn't the end.

1230
01:09:15,171 --> 01:09:16,305
- That's it.

1231
01:09:16,307 --> 01:09:17,876
This is just getting
worse and worse.

1232
01:09:17,878 --> 01:09:18,978
I'm getting out of this place.

1233
01:09:18,980 --> 01:09:21,383
Your granddad is
an absolute freak.

1234
01:09:21,385 --> 01:09:23,556
- But I don't want to die.

1235
01:09:24,592 --> 01:09:27,295
- Your death is
what's best for James.

1236
01:09:29,067 --> 01:09:29,969
- No.

1237
01:09:30,737 --> 01:09:33,040
(dramatic music)

1238
01:09:33,042 --> 01:09:35,110
- [Dudley] He's gone
mental and he has to die.

1239
01:09:35,112 --> 01:09:36,914
- [Geppetto] Fucking kid.

1240
01:09:36,916 --> 01:09:38,249
- I, I can't listen to him.

1241
01:09:38,251 --> 01:09:40,421
We need to save him.

1242
01:09:40,423 --> 01:09:43,495
(suspenseful music)

1243
01:09:45,298 --> 01:09:47,370
- James, help me please!

1244
01:09:50,543 --> 01:09:51,612
- Pinocchio?

1245
01:09:52,648 --> 01:09:55,486
- James, Mia,
Father's gone crazy.

1246
01:09:57,023 --> 01:09:59,358
- I know. I don't
want you to die.

1247
01:09:59,360 --> 01:10:01,564
Okay? You're in danger.

1248
01:10:01,566 --> 01:10:03,500
(suspenseful music)

1249
01:10:03,502 --> 01:10:04,903
- James! Mia!

1250
01:10:04,905 --> 01:10:05,807
Help me!

1251
01:10:07,275 --> 01:10:08,778
(gunshot blasts)

1252
01:10:08,780 --> 01:10:10,047
(Mia screams)
- Oh!

1253
01:10:10,049 --> 01:10:10,951
- Oh fuck!

1254
01:10:12,654 --> 01:10:15,491
(both gasping)

1255
01:10:15,493 --> 01:10:18,232
(ominous music)

1256
01:10:28,987 --> 01:10:30,055
- You bitch.

1257
01:10:32,728 --> 01:10:35,230
(vomit bubbles)

1258
01:10:35,232 --> 01:10:38,038
(gunshot blasts)

1259
01:10:39,040 --> 01:10:40,209
- Dudley, no!

1260
01:10:41,310 --> 01:10:44,150
(dramatic music)

1261
01:10:45,252 --> 01:10:47,288
- [Mia] He locked the door.

1262
01:10:47,290 --> 01:10:48,758
- Untie me quick.
- Now!

1263
01:10:48,760 --> 01:10:51,062
- I know somewhere we can hide.

1264
01:10:51,064 --> 01:10:52,666
- No, no, no, no.
- Down there.

1265
01:10:52,668 --> 01:10:54,001
- We have to go. Now.
- James!

1266
01:10:54,003 --> 01:10:55,638
They have to die!

1267
01:10:55,640 --> 01:10:58,109
- Wait for me!
- I have no choice.

1268
01:10:58,111 --> 01:10:59,646
(dramatic music)

1269
01:10:59,648 --> 01:11:02,084
- [Pinocchio] Guys! Guys!

1270
01:11:02,086 --> 01:11:07,063
(dramatic music)
(thunder rumbling)

1271
01:11:07,798 --> 01:11:10,035
(mysterious music)

1272
01:11:13,141 --> 01:11:16,212
(lock clicking)

1273
01:11:16,214 --> 01:11:18,216
(ax thwacks)
(Mia screams)

1274
01:11:18,218 --> 01:11:20,989
(dramatic music)

1275
01:11:20,991 --> 01:11:21,924
(ax thwacking)

1276
01:11:21,926 --> 01:11:23,526
- Hide! Come on!

1277
01:11:23,528 --> 01:11:28,605
(ax thwacking)
(dramatic music)

1278
01:11:35,152 --> 01:11:38,791
- You killed Dudley!
I fucking hate you!

1279
01:11:38,793 --> 01:11:40,728
- Shh, shh, shh, shh.

1280
01:11:40,730 --> 01:11:43,300
It's okay. I can bring
Dudley back, boy.

1281
01:11:43,302 --> 01:11:47,409
I can bring Dudley back and
I'll bring Mia back too.

1282
01:11:47,411 --> 01:11:50,614
James, James, this
was all for you, boy.

1283
01:11:50,616 --> 01:11:51,616
- No it wasn't. No it wasn't.

1284
01:11:51,618 --> 01:11:52,686
No it wasn't. No it wasn't.

1285
01:11:52,688 --> 01:11:55,123
- You disobeyed me, James.

1286
01:11:55,125 --> 01:11:57,127
Do you think those friends
wouldn't say anything?

1287
01:11:57,129 --> 01:11:58,598
They're children!

1288
01:11:59,567 --> 01:12:01,569
(ominous music)
(thunder rumbling)

1289
01:12:01,571 --> 01:12:03,340
- You're a monster!

1290
01:12:03,342 --> 01:12:04,275
(Geppetto breathing heavily)

1291
01:12:04,277 --> 01:12:05,778
- Let me in.

1292
01:12:05,780 --> 01:12:07,449
Let me in, James.

1293
01:12:07,451 --> 01:12:09,251
- No.
- Let me in.

1294
01:12:09,253 --> 01:12:11,390
- No! I fucking hate you!

1295
01:12:11,392 --> 01:12:12,892
- Let me in!

1296
01:12:12,894 --> 01:12:15,431
Open the fucking door!

1297
01:12:15,433 --> 01:12:17,469
(Geppetto shouting)

1298
01:12:17,471 --> 01:12:20,475
Now you're ruining everything!

1299
01:12:20,477 --> 01:12:22,414
Get out of the way, boy.

1300
01:12:23,483 --> 01:12:26,420
Get away from the
fucking door, kid!

1301
01:12:26,422 --> 01:12:31,499
(dramatic music)
(door banging)

1302
01:12:32,033 --> 01:12:34,471
(rain pattering)

1303
01:12:37,209 --> 01:12:40,182
(thunder rumbling)

1304
01:12:41,618 --> 01:12:42,521
Mia!

1305
01:12:48,165 --> 01:12:51,235
(water splashing)

1306
01:12:51,237 --> 01:12:53,810
(ax scraping)

1307
01:12:56,314 --> 01:12:57,216
Mia!

1308
01:13:01,257 --> 01:13:02,892
(puppet creaking)

1309
01:13:02,894 --> 01:13:03,796
Come out.

1310
01:13:05,599 --> 01:13:06,502
Come out.

1311
01:13:08,906 --> 01:13:10,977
Come on, boys and girls.

1312
01:13:11,912 --> 01:13:14,048
(Pinocchio gasping)

1313
01:13:14,050 --> 01:13:16,789
(rain pattering)

1314
01:13:18,191 --> 01:13:20,727
I'm on the cusp of
something great.

1315
01:13:20,729 --> 01:13:22,534
Something bigger than you both.

1316
01:13:25,305 --> 01:13:28,209
(ax scraping)

1317
01:13:28,211 --> 01:13:30,815
You know I can't let you win.

1318
01:13:30,817 --> 01:13:31,718
No way.

1319
01:13:32,888 --> 01:13:35,759
Dr. Gammon showed me how
to bring you all back.

1320
01:13:38,031 --> 01:13:40,603
(ax scraping)

1321
01:13:45,712 --> 01:13:48,786
(Geppetto laughing)

1322
01:14:03,148 --> 01:14:04,281
(dramatic music)

1323
01:14:04,283 --> 01:14:06,956
(Mia shouting)

1324
01:14:08,325 --> 01:14:10,997
(ax thwacking)

1325
01:14:15,339 --> 01:14:17,307
(Geppetto spits)

1326
01:14:17,309 --> 01:14:18,544
(dramatic music)

1327
01:14:18,546 --> 01:14:20,950
(Mia yells)

1328
01:14:21,852 --> 01:14:23,721
You ruined everything.

1329
01:14:23,723 --> 01:14:27,395
(punches thudding)

1330
01:14:27,397 --> 01:14:28,899
It's time to die.

1331
01:14:29,800 --> 01:14:32,773
(punches thudding)

1332
01:14:36,014 --> 01:14:39,218
(ominous music)

1333
01:14:39,220 --> 01:14:44,297
(Geppetto grunts)
(Mia shouts)

1334
01:14:45,165 --> 01:14:47,769
(Mia screaming)
(ominous music)

1335
01:14:47,771 --> 01:14:50,008
You can all be my puppets!

1336
01:14:51,344 --> 01:14:54,416
(ominous music)

1337
01:14:54,418 --> 01:14:55,584
(thunder rumbles)
(Mia screams)

1338
01:14:55,586 --> 01:15:00,663
(dramatic music)
(Geppetto shouts)

1339
01:15:01,665 --> 01:15:03,335
- Leave them alone.

1340
01:15:06,809 --> 01:15:08,211
- What the fuck?

1341
01:15:10,115 --> 01:15:11,950
- You forget yourself.

1342
01:15:11,952 --> 01:15:13,119
I made you.

1343
01:15:13,121 --> 01:15:15,323
- I'm not your puppet anymore.

1344
01:15:15,325 --> 01:15:16,560
- Yes you are.

1345
01:15:16,562 --> 01:15:18,897
Without me you're
just a piece of wood.

1346
01:15:18,899 --> 01:15:20,901
- No! I'm more than that.

1347
01:15:20,903 --> 01:15:22,839
- A puppet needs a master.

1348
01:15:22,841 --> 01:15:25,110
And I'm the only one
that can make you real.

1349
01:15:25,112 --> 01:15:27,347
Make you like James.

1350
01:15:27,349 --> 01:15:29,886
- I don't wanna be
like James anymore.

1351
01:15:29,888 --> 01:15:32,257
I just wanna be me.

1352
01:15:32,259 --> 01:15:34,896
- And you're always
gonna be hollow inside.

1353
01:15:34,898 --> 01:15:38,169
Incomplete, splintered,
and cracked.

1354
01:15:38,171 --> 01:15:39,672
- Pinocchio, don't listen.

1355
01:15:39,674 --> 01:15:43,447
- You, you can't
control me anymore.

1356
01:15:43,449 --> 01:15:45,618
- I gave you life!

1357
01:15:45,620 --> 01:15:47,922
I'm not only your
father, Pinocchio,

1358
01:15:47,924 --> 01:15:49,057
I'm your God!

1359
01:15:49,059 --> 01:15:53,132
And your God 'til I fucking die!

1360
01:15:53,134 --> 01:15:54,469
- Fuck you!

1361
01:15:54,471 --> 01:15:55,838
(dramatic music)

1362
01:15:55,840 --> 01:15:56,742
- Goodbye.

1363
01:15:57,977 --> 01:15:58,879
God.

1364
01:15:59,916 --> 01:16:03,252
(gunshot blasts)
(dramatic music)

1365
01:16:03,254 --> 01:16:06,660
(James gasping)

1366
01:16:06,662 --> 01:16:09,801
(cage door creaking)

1367
01:16:11,137 --> 01:16:14,542
(dramatic music)
(Geppetto screams)

1368
01:16:14,544 --> 01:16:16,011
- Holy fuck.
- Whoa!

1369
01:16:16,013 --> 01:16:18,216
- Holy fuck.
- Ah!

1370
01:16:18,218 --> 01:16:21,556
(dramatic music)
(Geppetto's body thuds)

1371
01:16:21,558 --> 01:16:26,568
(ominous music)
(puppet growling)

1372
01:16:27,770 --> 01:16:30,574
(sparks hissing)

1373
01:16:30,576 --> 01:16:33,415
(dramatic music)

1374
01:16:37,022 --> 01:16:40,059
- James, we need to go.
- Come on!

1375
01:16:40,061 --> 01:16:42,901
(dramatic music)

1376
01:16:45,974 --> 01:16:48,946
(flames crackling)

1377
01:16:54,457 --> 01:16:56,793
(solemn music)

1378
01:16:56,795 --> 01:17:00,803
- James, are we still friends?

1379
01:17:04,711 --> 01:17:05,844
(gentle piano music)

1380
01:17:05,846 --> 01:17:08,184
Am I bad?

1381
01:17:10,823 --> 01:17:12,858
- You were just confused.

1382
01:17:12,860 --> 01:17:15,433
Just don't do it again, okay?

1383
01:17:16,300 --> 01:17:17,870
- I'm such a rascal, aren't I?

1384
01:17:19,306 --> 01:17:20,808
(Mia laughs)

1385
01:17:20,810 --> 01:17:23,312
- Yeah, besides, I mean they
were all assholes anyway.

1386
01:17:23,314 --> 01:17:26,118
Oh, except my dentist.

1387
01:17:26,120 --> 01:17:28,690
I'm gonna need a new dentist.

1388
01:17:28,692 --> 01:17:30,027
(Mia laughs)

1389
01:17:30,029 --> 01:17:31,163
- I'll get them too.

1390
01:17:32,066 --> 01:17:35,236
(James and Mia laughing)

1391
01:17:35,238 --> 01:17:38,412
You won't tell people
about me, will you?

1392
01:17:42,587 --> 01:17:43,489
- No lie.

1393
01:17:44,591 --> 01:17:46,158
- [Pinocchio] Good. Me too.

1394
01:17:46,160 --> 01:17:48,497
(distant siren wailing)

1395
01:17:48,499 --> 01:17:50,701
(Pinocchio giggles)
(mysterious music)

1396
01:17:50,703 --> 01:17:52,440
- Come on. Let's go.

1397
01:17:56,481 --> 01:17:57,884
- I'll catch up.

1398
01:18:02,527 --> 01:18:05,900
(sighs) Goodbye Father.

1399
01:18:07,070 --> 01:18:09,641
You made me. You can't
control me anymore.

1400
01:18:10,710 --> 01:18:12,310
James is mine.

1401
01:18:12,312 --> 01:18:15,152
(flames roaring)

1402
01:18:17,123 --> 01:18:20,529
(Wood Mother screaming)

1403
01:18:21,465 --> 01:18:24,368
- [Wood Mother] You Pinocchio!

1404
01:18:24,370 --> 01:18:26,038
(mysterious music)

1405
01:18:26,040 --> 01:18:28,577
- I didn't enjoy having to
kill them people, you know.

1406
01:18:28,579 --> 01:18:31,585
(mysterious music)

1407
01:19:11,009 --> 01:19:13,981
(Cricket coughing)

1408
01:19:17,588 --> 01:19:19,823
- That, that bloody kid.

1409
01:19:19,825 --> 01:19:24,235
I might be small, but I
have big plans for this one.

1410
01:19:25,070 --> 01:19:27,875
From roots come resurrection.

1411
01:19:29,311 --> 01:19:30,847
I'll bring you back, my master.

1412
01:19:32,284 --> 01:19:35,123
(dramatic music)

1413
01:19:40,815 --> 01:19:42,850
- This is behind the scenes.

1414
01:19:42,852 --> 01:19:44,286
And action.

1415
01:19:44,288 --> 01:19:45,589
Go on, go on, go on.

1416
01:19:45,591 --> 01:19:48,261
Oh!
(crew members chattering)

1417
01:19:48,263 --> 01:19:49,466
And roll camera.

1418
01:19:50,601 --> 01:19:51,638
- What's this?

1419
01:19:52,438 --> 01:19:54,807
(crew members laughing)

1420
01:19:54,809 --> 01:19:56,878
- High five?
- High five.

1421
01:19:56,880 --> 01:19:57,980
- Yeah.
- How's she doing?

1422
01:19:57,982 --> 01:19:59,684
- It's Kelly's stunt double.

1423
01:19:59,686 --> 01:20:01,922
(crew members laughing)

1424
01:20:01,924 --> 01:20:03,592
(bright music)

1425
01:20:03,594 --> 01:20:04,496
Yep.

1426
01:20:06,032 --> 01:20:08,203
And action on the coffin.

1427
01:20:09,238 --> 01:20:10,539
(Wood Mother coughing)

1428
01:20:10,541 --> 01:20:11,443
Action!

1429
01:20:15,851 --> 01:20:16,918
Roll sound.

1430
01:20:16,920 --> 01:20:18,256
- Open your mouth.
- Action.

1431
01:20:21,530 --> 01:20:23,130
Okay, camera set.

1432
01:20:23,132 --> 01:20:26,237
Here we go.
- It's taping too fast.

1433
01:20:26,239 --> 01:20:28,441
(crew members chattering)

1434
01:20:28,443 --> 01:20:30,615
In three, two, one, bang!

1435
01:20:31,718 --> 01:20:36,628
(playful music)
(crew members chattering)

1436
01:20:37,528 --> 01:20:38,530
And sparks.

1437
01:20:39,667 --> 01:20:42,070
What you doing today, Vince?

1438
01:20:43,507 --> 01:20:46,377
- Well, just a whole-
- Relax.

1439
01:20:46,379 --> 01:20:48,683
- Yeah, I think
that's great, guys.

1440
01:20:48,685 --> 01:20:51,120
Well done.
(cart rattling)

1441
01:20:51,122 --> 01:20:54,259
(light piano music)
- Yeah, as you go in,

1442
01:20:54,261 --> 01:20:55,764
you then bring the foot.

1443
01:20:55,766 --> 01:20:57,232
- Yeah.
- Okay.

1444
01:20:57,234 --> 01:20:59,002
- [Crew Member] Maybe could
someone hold the head?

1445
01:20:59,004 --> 01:21:00,806
Would that help? I don't know.

1446
01:21:00,808 --> 01:21:03,713
- I think you see the head.
(crew members laughing)

1447
01:21:03,715 --> 01:21:06,686
- Hang on, wait a minute.
- Look at the arm.

1448
01:21:06,688 --> 01:21:07,588
- Chopped off.

1449
01:21:09,526 --> 01:21:11,462
- Oh fuck, my arm! Help!

1450
01:21:13,199 --> 01:21:15,368
(crew members chattering)
- Action.

1451
01:21:15,370 --> 01:21:16,203
Maybe he's like a spy.

1452
01:21:16,205 --> 01:21:17,107
He's looking around.

1453
01:21:19,378 --> 01:21:20,514
Like that, pointing it.

1454
01:21:24,221 --> 01:21:26,323
And three.

1455
01:21:26,325 --> 01:21:29,800
(crew members chattering)

1456
01:21:31,435 --> 01:21:32,706
- Good luck.
- I'm done.

1457
01:21:34,007 --> 01:21:36,748
(playful music)

1458
01:21:38,249 --> 01:21:39,787
- So you okay? Ready?
- Okay.

1459
01:21:41,923 --> 01:21:42,925
Okay, drop.

1460
01:21:48,269 --> 01:21:50,037
Professional film crew.

1461
01:21:50,039 --> 01:21:53,045
(puppeteer laughs)